     1	r"""Per-rover mission FSM (v2, after Astra Gate 3).  One `RoverAgent` per rover; the Supervisor owns planning
     2	services (`AgentContext`), reservations and the safety layers.
     3	
     4	Task = deliver one cube colour.  A task executes its PushPlan one leg at a time and REPLANS from the observed
     5	cube state after every leg (a stale plan is never executed).
     6	
     7	    IDLE -> NAVIGATE -> ALIGN -> CAPTURE -> VERIFY_CAPTURE -> PUSH -> MEASURE --(more legs)--> RETREAT -> replan
     8	                                                                              \--(final)--> VERIFY_DELIVERY -> RETREAT
     9	                                                                                            -> CONFIRM -> IDLE
    10	    interrupts: WAIT (blocked) | RELOCALIZE (estimate unsafe) | EMERGENCY_STOP (safety layer) | YIELD (parking)
    11	
    12	Invariants
    13	- `engaged` (the channel may hold a cube) is independent of the state and survives every interrupt.  While
    14	  engaged the only permitted motions are the manipulation itself (capture/push along the committed line) or a
    15	  STRAIGHT retreat.  It clears only after a retreat whose measured backward displacement reached the distance.
    16	- Every failure path increments a bounded per-task budget; every state has a timeout; no state waits forever.
    17	"""
